26. Most Important Financial Rule

Financial data must be traceable.

For every contribution or payment, the system should be able to answer:

> Who contributed what, when, through which payment mechanism, what external transaction confirmed it, and how was it reflected in the Chama's financial records?



The system must therefore distinguish between:

Contribution
     │
     ▼
Payment
     │
     ▼
Payment Attempt
     │
     ▼
Provider Transaction
     │
     ▼
Ledger Entry

Bank-side reconciliation is a separate process:

Bank Account
     │
     ▼
Bank Transaction
     │
     ▼
Reconciliation Record
     │
     ▼
Ledger Entry

Successful financial transactions should not simply be deleted. Corrections should use appropriate reversal, refund or adjustment mechanisms.


