28. Project Development Rule

> Build only what the current version requires, but design the boundaries so future versions can be added without rewriting the core system.



This means:

Do not build microservices before they are needed.

Do not integrate every payment provider at once.

Do not add Kafka/event streaming without a real requirement.

Do not couple the Chama domain directly to a payment provider.

Do not treat financial balances as arbitrary mutable values.

Do not sacrifice correctness for development speed.

Do not build features without validated requirements.


The architecture should be simple enough for the current product and structured enough to evolve safely.

